<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>DW - English for Africa</title><subtitle type="html">News, Analysis and Service from Germany and Europe - in 30 Languages</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa</id><updated>2026-11-03T07:01:16Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-africa" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12756?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>US to drop South Africa, Rwanda from duty-free trade initiative</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f5e92f234e9b4f9e780f07f04247d667e0c5abfe00e47cd38f932356d1f740d</id><updated>2026-11-03T07:01:16Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T21:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-to-drop-south-africa-rwanda-from-duty-free-trade-initiative/a-79834508--6eef768d2e5a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-to-drop-south-africa-rwanda-from-duty-free-trade-initiative/a-79834508?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Trump administration has said South Africa and Rwanda are breaking the rules of the AGOA free trade initiative, a centerpiece of US economic engagement with sub-Saharan Africa.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Uganda begins withdrawing troops from Somalia after two decades</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:168de86d4ba5b0df0ddfd7ee3774abe923a785237b92d6b6c960b3192bf96a2a</id><updated>2026-11-03T07:00:16Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T12:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uganda-begins-withdrawing-troops-from-somalia-after-two-decades/a-79829903--679d18eec17e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uganda-begins-withdrawing-troops-from-somalia-after-two-decades/a-79829903?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ugandan troops first deployed to Somalia in 2007 as part of an international military coalition to battle Islamic insurgents. But the mission has faced mounting pressure since a US decision to withdraw funding.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Will renewed conflict derail Ethiopia's economic growth?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a102b677a2e73eff4237197713f83d563ac813a66d55aafcdb1dbe82aa63160a</id><updated>2026-11-03T07:00:16Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T11:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-renewed-conflict-derail-ethiopia-s-economic-growth/a-79807060--aec9783cc542.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-renewed-conflict-derail-ethiopia-s-economic-growth/a-79807060?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ethiopia's economy is growing strongly. But renewed fighting in the north of the BRICS member state could deter investment, strain public finances and push up the cost of living.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Human trafficking victims stranded in Guinea-Bissau</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b40c3cff8aebde971c3e21571596b51e98f331c71c563e73c5d2458fb0992ae8</id><updated>2026-11-03T07:00:16Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T14:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/human-trafficking-victims-stranded-in-guinea-bissau/a-79785558--af9688fcc3e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/human-trafficking-victims-stranded-in-guinea-bissau/a-79785558?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Dozens of West Africans lured to Guinea-Bissau with promises of jobs and migration to Europe say they were exploited by a suspected trafficking network. Now many cannot afford to return home.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
